    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "For what values of $x$ does the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+1$ lie between $y=-1$ and $y=2$?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$-4<x<2$",
      "worked": "The line lies between the two levels when $-1<y<2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}-1&<\\frac{1}{2}x+1<2\\\\-2&<\\frac{1}{2}x<1\\\\-4&<x<2\\end{align*}$$",
